        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Many people wake up to an alarm clock."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "But how did people wake up before alarm clocks were invented?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "They used a knocker-up."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Knocker-ups were people."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Factories hired them to wake up workers."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Knocker-ups were often elderly people or police officers."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "They would knock on people's windows."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "They had many tools."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "They often used bamboo sticks, small stones, or peashooters."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "In the 20th century, knocker-ups started disappearing."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "They lost their jobs because of alarm clocks."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Alarm clocks were cheaper and more reliable."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "What are some other jobs that have disappeared?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
